      "bottlenose_dolphins_have_been_document": "Bottlenose dolphins have been documented bashing octopuses against the seafloor to subdue them before eating — a learned behavior.",
      "bottlenose_dolphins_have_been_document_2": "Bottlenose dolphins have been documented chasing octopuses — and learning to bash them against the seafloor to subdue them before eating. The behavior is socially transmitted within pods.",
      "brain_coral": "Brain Coral",
      "brain_corals_can_live_900_years_and_gr": "Brain corals can live 900+ years and grow 10 m wide. They're older than most cathedrals.",
      "brain_is_centralized_in_the_skull_spin": "Brain is centralized in the skull. Spinal cord carries signals to + from peripheral body. Limbs follow commands; they don't generate behavior independently. Vertebrate body plan: brain decides, body obeys.",
      "brain_is_distributed_1_3_in_head_2_3_i": "Brain is distributed: ~1/3 in head, ~2/3 in 8 arm ganglia. Each arm has working memory + sensory autonomy + can decide-act locally. Central brain takes summaries + handles big picture. Cephalopod body plan: parallel processing, embodied cognition.",
      "branching_coral": "Branching Coral",
