      "jikji_korea": "Jikji (Korea)",
      "jikji_used_sand_mold_casting_less_repe": "Jikji used sand-mold casting (less repeatable). Gutenberg used the hand-mold + copper matrix (very repeatable). Repeatability matters when you need 50,000 identical sorts.",
      "joad_raymond_ed_the_cambridge_companio": "Joad Raymond, ed., The Cambridge Companion to British Civil War Print (2015)",
      "johann_carolus_had_been_writing_handwr": "Johann Carolus had been writing handwritten newsletters by hand for a small subscription audience (wealthy merchants + diplomats) since the 1590s. By 1604 he had so many subscribers that hand-copying was unsustainable. He bought a press, started printing the newsletter as the Relation, and petitioned the Strasbourg city council in late 1605 for a printing monopoly. The petition (which survives) is the founding document of the newspaper as a form.",
      "johannes_gutenberg_mainz_germany": "Johannes Gutenberg, Mainz, Germany",
      "johnson_1755": "Johnson (1755)",
      "johnson_s_1755_dictionary_webster_oed_": "Johnson's 1755 dictionary → Webster → OED → Merriam-Webster online. How language gets standardized into print.",
