      "with_care": "with care",
      "within_20_years_similar_papers_had_app": "Within 20 years similar papers had appeared in Wolfenbüttel (1609), Amsterdam (1618), London (1622), Cologne (1620), Berlin (1626), Hamburg (1630), Stockholm (1645), and Boston (1704). The form spread fast once one printer had proven it worked.",
      "within_40_years_of_the_gutenberg_bible": "Within 40 years of the Gutenberg Bible, every major category of book we still print had at least one printed exemplar: scripture, scholarship, classics, dictionaries, vernacular literature, illustrated books, reference, travel writing, popular illustration. The press did not just produce more books; it discovered what books could be.",
      "without_antimony_the_lead_tin_alloy_sh": "Without antimony, the lead-tin alloy shrinks as it cools. Cast type comes out smaller than the matrix with rounded edges. Letters are unreadable. This is exactly why pre-Gutenberg attempts at metal type failed.",
